<h1 class="page-title" data-page-title-uuid="0b75b842-ba60-8131-881b-f4b981d5c44a">Bridge Operations Handbook <a class="source-link" href="https://www.notion.so/b1d6e00017014d008000000000000001" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">↗</a></h1>

# Mission Overview

The USS Enterprise-D is on a deep-space survey near the Romulan Neutral Zone. Coordinate any sensor sweeps with Data before adjusting sensor gain.

> 🖖 Captain on the bridge: [Jean-Luc Picard](mailto:jean-luc.picard@enterprise.starfleet.invalid "Jean-Luc Picard <jean-luc.picard@enterprise.starfleet.invalid>") presides over all standing orders below.
>
> These orders hold until the ship leaves the Neutral Zone or the captain rescinds them in writing.

## Crew Roster

- Duty roster lives at [Shift Roster](/chat/0b75b842-ba60-88dd-b090-baf44d88db59) — refer to it before bridge handoff.
- Senior staff:
  - **Command:** Jean-Luc Picard, William T. Riker
  - **Operations:** [Data](mailto:data@enterprise.starfleet.invalid "Data <data@enterprise.starfleet.invalid>"), [Geordi La Forge](mailto:geordi.laforge@enterprise.starfleet.invalid "Geordi La Forge <geordi.laforge@enterprise.starfleet.invalid>")
  - **Medical:** [Beverly Crusher](mailto:beverly.crusher@enterprise.starfleet.invalid "Beverly Crusher <beverly.crusher@enterprise.starfleet.invalid>")
1. Confirm shift assignments at start of duty.
2. File anomalies in the [Incident Log: Stardate 47988.1](/chat/0b75b842-ba60-80f0-ab79-7448df7f2124).
   1. Note the stardate and the station that saw it.
   2. Attach a sensor trace when there is one.

| Station | Relieved by |
| --- | --- |
| Conn | Ensign Ro Laren |
| Ops | Lieutenant Commander Data |

---

## Standing Orders

- [x] Maintain Yellow Alert posture in the Neutral Zone
- [ ] Run weekly warp-core diagnostic with [Geordi La Forge](mailto:geordi.laforge@enterprise.starfleet.invalid "Geordi La Forge <geordi.laforge@enterprise.starfleet.invalid>")
- [ ] Medical readiness drill on <time datetime="2369-04-20">Sun Apr 20th, 2369</time>

<details>

<summary><strong>Engagement protocols</strong></summary>

Hail before firing. Shields raised only after a second sensor confirmation.

- Tactical leads: Worf
- Weapons lock needs the captain's or first officer's word.

</details>

> Make it so.

```python
def hail(frequency):
    return f"Open channel {frequency}."
```

